# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secrets, account material and runtime state.
#
# The gateway writes here when it runs: `~/.workbuddy2dsh/auths/` holds
# plaintext access/refresh tokens. Nothing below may ever be committed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
auths/
data/
*.key
*.pem
*.env
.env
.env.*
config.json
config.local.json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Upstream source tree (a full checkout vendors the gateway; a release does not)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/login
/credit
/wb2api
/signin_bin
/backups/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Published build artifacts, deliberately TRACKED.
#
# `bin/` holds the gateway binary and `lib/` the browser half. Both are what a
# consumer needs with no build step of their own: `bin/` is the first place
# `defaultBinaryPath()` looks (src/paths.js), and `lib/client.js` is what the
# host's module loader registers the composer chip from. Neither is rebuilt at
# install time, so neither can be left to CI to produce.
#
# Build caches and scratch still stay out — see the `_tools/cache/` rules above.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.tmp
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
server.exe
.DS_Store

# Go toolchain and build caches — a full source checkout vendors these, and
# none of it belongs in a published repo.
/_tools/go/
/_tools/cache/
/_tools/tmp/
/_tools/gopath/
/_tools/go-toolchains/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# IDE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
LOOP.md
PLAN.md
SPEC.md

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Node
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
.npm/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Documentation.
#
# README.md, AGENTS.md and everything under docs/ are the published surface of
# this repo and MUST be versioned. Everything else is a scratch file.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.md
!README.md
!AGENTS.md
!docs/**
!LICENSE
!NOTICE

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vendored reference copies (not part of the build, safe to keep in a checkout)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/_upstream_bin/

# Local verification tooling
/cmd/desktopverify*/

# Local setup output the old script used to leave behind. Only `bin/` is a
# tracked, published location — see the note above.
/_runtime/

# Local analysis helpers kept for this machine's investigation work. The
# bundled Go toolchain and everything the setup script keeps inside it is
# covered by the cache rules above.
/_tools/
